          ],
          "level": 1,
          "content": "5 NUMBER PLAY"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.226,
            0.289,
            0.247
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 122"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.261,
            0.295,
            0.283
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.291,
            0.848,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "1. The sum of four consecutive numbers is 34. What are these numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.337,
            0.732,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** The required consecutive numbers are 7, 8, 9 and 10."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.367,
            0.847,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": "2. Suppose p is the greatest of five consecutive numbers. Describe the other four numbers in terms of p."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.412,
            0.847,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Given p is the greatest of five consecutive number, so other four are (p − 1), (p − 2), (p − 3) and (p − 4)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.468,
            0.848,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": "3. For each statement below, determine whether it is always true, sometimes true, or never true. Explain your answer. Mention examples and non-examples as appropriate. Justify your claim using algebra."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.547,
            0.727,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": "(i) The sum of two even numbers is a multiple of 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.577,
            0.847,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "(ii) If a number is not divisible by 18, then it is also not divisible by 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.625,
            0.848,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "(iii) If two numbers are not divisible by 6, then their sum is not divisible by 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.667,
            0.848,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "(iv) The sum of a multiple of 6 and a multiple of 9 is a multiple of 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.211,
            0.715,
            0.844,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "(v) The sum of a multiple of 6 and a multiple of 3 is a multiple of 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.75,
            0.204,
            0.767
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.216,
            0.767,
            0.42,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "(i) Sometimes true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.786,
            0.619,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "2 + 4 = 6, 4 + 8 = 12 are multiples of 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.806,
            0.695,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": "but 2 + 6 = 8, 6 + 8 = 14 are not multiples of 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.83,
            0.421,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Sometimes true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.85,
            0.607,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "30 is not divisible by both 18 and 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.87,
            0.676,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": "27 is not divisible by 18, but divisible by 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.864,
            0.918,
            0.879,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": "1"
        }
      ]
    }
